# Architecture

```
HTTP (thin)  ->  Game service / tools  ->  Eloquent models  ->  Postgres
UI (React)   ->  Inertia page props / JSON API                 (display only)
```

- Controllers validate input and delegate. No game rules in controllers.
- Tools are the only agent-facing surface. Adding a game capability means adding a tool.
- Models hold persistence and small derived helpers (`toGameArray`). No HTTP awareness.
- Prefer plain PHP services over events/queues until a real need appears.
- No abstraction with a single implementation. No interfaces invented for tests alone.
- Migrations are append-only once merged. Rename by adding, backfilling, then removing.
- Integer math for game numbers. Never floats for HP, damage, gold, or XP.

If a change needs a new layer, justify it in the commit message in one sentence.
